// game.c — "skill-issue": minimalist low-poly tactical FPS prototype, Phase 1.
//
// One C23 translation unit, two backends selected at compile time:
//   Server  (--server) : dedicated sim + UDP, no GL/audio/window. --directory
//                        runs the instance directory. Live client<->server
//                        multiplayer over UDP (§6): Quick Join, prediction,
//                        interpolation, friend codes — all in this one binary.
//   Windows (game.exe) : borderless fullscreen popup window + WGL core 3.3.
//                        No display-mode change and no exclusive fullscreen,
//                        so no HDR mode-switch black screens and alt-tab is a
//                        plain DWM window switch. First frame is rendered
//                        *before* the window is shown (no startup flash).
//   Linux   (game)     : TWO modes in one binary, chosen at RUNTIME.
//                        No arguments = play: X11 window (borderless
//                        fullscreen via the EWMH hint), EGL core 3.3, raw
//                        mouse through XInput2, sound through ALSA — all of
//                        libXi and libasound reached by dlopen so a missing
//                        one degrades instead of failing to start. This is
//                        what `make deploy` scp's to the handheld.
//                        --do/--script = the headless CLI harness: EGL
//                        surfaceless on Mesa llvmpipe, renders into an FBO,
//                        driven by a tiny script language (see usage() below)
//                        that can press keys, move the mouse, dump
//                        screenshots (PNG) and print movement traces. The two
//                        modes are mutually exclusive at main(), which is what
//                        keeps every proof command deterministic.
//
// The frame loop itself belongs to NEITHER backend: app_start/app_frame/
// app_sync (just above the platform split) hold everything between "here is dt
// and the input state" and "swap the buffers", because a second windowed
// backend is exactly how a tick accumulator and a press-latch rule end up
// existing twice with one of the copies subtly wrong.
//
// Shared core: config (config.cfg next to the executable), seeded procedural
// map (AABB solids), fixed-timestep player sim (120 Hz) with render
// interpolation, GL 3.3 core renderer (one static VBO for the world, one
// dynamic VBO for the HUD), and the "GRATICULE" UI: a procedural SDF
// typeface (Hershey-simplex skeletons baked to a distance atlas at GL init)
// plus rounded-panel/capsule/ruler primitives, all in the one HUD batch.
//
// C23 gotcha (verified in-container): MinGW-w64 stddef.h lacks unreachable();
// constexpr/nullptr/typed enums work on both compilers. #embed needs GCC 15.
//
// MAP OF THE FILE. One TU is a deliberate constraint, not an accident, but
// twelve thousand lines need an index. Every entry below is a banner comment
// you can search for verbatim; they appear in this order, and the order is
// forced by C — a helper is defined above its first use.
//
//   GL 3.3 core loader             GL_FUNC_LIST X-macro; add entry points there
//   Math                           column-major mat4, y-up RH, yaw 0 -> -z
//   PCG32                          separate streams: map/gun/bot/vfx/synth
//   Config                         "key value" lines; MV_/WP_/ACTION_DEF tables
//   Procedural map                 AABB solids = collision set AND render mesh
//   Events                         the sim's one-way channel to presentation
//   Hitscan                        ray vs AABB, shared by every shot and probe
//   Procedural audio               15 sounds synthesized at startup, seeded
//   THE CONFIRMATION MATRIX        hit/kill x body/head as TWO axes, not four
//   Audio routing                  which event becomes which sound, and where
//   Player sim                     fixed 120 Hz, per-axis AABB, lean, slide
//   Locomotion                     ONE mv_* set for the player AND every bot
//   Skeleton locomotion            procedural anim; feet are the ground truth
//   Bots + deathmatch              AI, tactics, match state, damage, respawn
//   Weapon                         ONE gun_shoot for whoever pulls the trigger
//   Renderer                       world/scene/HUD VBOs, shadow map, sky, PBR
//   UI batch                       one draw call for all HUD and menu geometry
//   Settings menu                  immediate mode: layout+hit-test+draw in one
//   VFX + dynamic scene batch      figures, tracers, marks; lifetimes in TICKS
//   Audio analysis                 the numbers that stand in for listening
//   Frame step                     app_frame/app_sync: the loop, shared
//   Linux headless backend         EGL surfaceless + the script harness
//   Linux native backend           X11 + EGL + XInput2 + ALSA, the played path
//   Windows backend                WGL, raw input, WASAPI, the frame loop
//
// The proof commands (figcheck / vmcheck / vmsight / mapcheck / parity / kine /
// lean / budget / tacstat) live in the harness and are documented in --help;
// CLAUDE.md explains what defect each one exists to catch.

#define _DEFAULT_SOURCE  // readlink/strdup despite -std=c23 strict mode

